{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01JqqAzy5HRvJyA4DZ9GnjCm", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.02155\"}, {\"url\": \"https://cl-informatik-new.uibk.ac.at/images/publications_pdf/2017/formal_proof_of_the_kepler_conjecture.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://code.google.com/p/flyspeck\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/~jrh13/papers/kepler.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/flyspeck/flyspeck\"}, {\"url\": \"https://ar5iv.arxiv.org/html/1501.02155\"}, {\"url\": \"https://experimentalmath.info/blog/2014/08/formal-proof-completed-for-keplers-conjecture-on-sphere-packing/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://sugaku.net/oa/A5113539451\"}, {\"url\": \"https://experimentalmath.info/blog/?p=6503\"}, {\"url\": \"https://experimentalmath.info/blog/2014/08/\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:06:08.907Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Flyspeck project completed formal proof Kepler conjecture year", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01XtoBFYmCbFea7mUmSuq7mP", "content": [{"title": "A formal proof of the Kepler conjecture", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.02155"}, {"title": "formal proof of the kepler conjecture", "url": "https://cl-informatik-new.uibk.ac.at/images/publications_pdf/2017/formal_proof_of_the_kepler_conjecture.pdf"}, {"title": "code.google.com", "url": "https://code.google.com/p/flyspeck"}, {"title": "A Formal Proof of the Kepler Conjecture", "url": "https://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/~jrh13/papers/kepler.html"}, {"title": "github.com", "url": "https://github.com/flyspeck/flyspeck"}, {"title": "A formal proof of the Kepler conjecture", "url": "https://ar5iv.arxiv.org/html/1501.02155"}, {"title": "Formal proof completed for Kepler’s conjecture on sphere packing", "url": "https://experimentalmath.info/blog/2014/08/formal-proof-completed-for-keplers-conjecture-on-sphere-packing/"}, {"title": "Thomas C. Hales", "url": "https://sugaku.net/oa/A5113539451"}, {"title": "Formal proof completed for Kepler’s conjecture on sphere packing", "url": "https://experimentalmath.info/blog/?p=6503"}, {"title": "Opportunities and challenges in experimental mathematics", "url": "https://experimentalmath.info/blog/2014/08/"}]}, "The Flyspeck project was completed in 2014, on August 10. Thomas Hales announced the completion that day, and the project's GitHub repository and the official published account both give that date.\n\n- **Completion date:** The project's GitHub page records the completion date as August 10, 2014.\n- **Who announced it:** A blog report says a team led by Thomas Hales of the University of Pittsburgh announced that their decade-long effort to construct a computer-verified formal proof of the Kepler conjecture was now complete.\n- **Scope:** The formalization covered both the textual arguments and the parts implemented as computer calculations. It was done in a combination of HOL Light and Isabelle proof assistants. This article describes a formal proof of the Kepler conjecture on dense sphere packings in a combination of the HOL Light and Isabelle proof assistants.\n- **Official account:** The paper constitutes the official published account of the now completed Flyspeck project. It appeared on arXiv as 1501.02155 in 2015.\n\nBackground: Hales began the project in 2003 after the original 2003 proof was published without full certification from referees. Hales had estimated that it would take 20 years to complete."], "durationSeconds": 4.580265625, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01JqqAzy5HRvJyA4DZ9GnjCm", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
